# /mcp status command, deterministic and LLM-free. Proves the .mcp.json
# auto-merge, the /mcp command path, and the zag.detach status worker survive
# end to end, AND that the status text now reaches the grid as a toast.
#
# Setup (via the parameterized launcher): a fixture HOME plus a project dir
# whose .mcp.json declares a SECOND server (jsonsrv, standard command-string +
# args shape) alongside the Lua-declared `fake`. The launcher cd's into that
# project dir before exec'ing zag, so zag's cwd-relative .mcp.json read merges
# jsonsrv on the first coroutine-context config load (which /mcp triggers).
#
# GRID-VISIBLE STATUS: zag.notify (the channel /mcp uses) now renders as a
# transient top-right toast in the TUI, on top of the still-written .lua_user
# log line. The status text lands in that toast, so we anchor on it directly.
# wait_text is SUBSTRING-ONLY (the /.../ delimiters are stripped, no regex):
#   * "MCP: " (uppercase, colon-space) cannot collide with the typed lowercase
#     "/mcp" prompt echo -- it only appears in the toast header.
#   * "jsonsrv" is never typed; it comes solely from the merged .mcp.json, so a
#     match proves the merge ran and the status reached the grid.
# Toast ttl for an info-level notify is 4s, so the wait_text steps sit
# immediately after the /mcp send to catch the toast inside its lifetime.
#
# The status text is also still in the fixture log under
# $ZAG_SIM_MCP_HOME/.zag/logs/<uuid>.log as
#   [lua_user] info: [notify] MCP: 0/2 servers, 0 tools
#   ○ fake (not connected)
#   ○ jsonsrv (not connected)
# (the toast is transient; the log is the durable record). The grid assertion
# below is the stronger of the two, so the log-side check is left as this note.
#
# A /mcp that wedged the detach worker, crashed on the .mcp.json merge, or
# left the TUI unresponsive would surface here as a wait_text timeout or a
# non-clean exit (the final /quit + wait_exit would time out or report a crash).

set env ZAG_SIM_MCP_HOME=/tmp/zag-sim-mcp-status-home
set env ZAG_SIM_MCP_PROJECT_DIR=/tmp/zag-sim-mcp-status-proj
spawn ./src/sim/scenarios/testdata/mcp_launch.sh
wait_text /Welcome to zag/
wait_idle 500ms
send "/mcp" <Enter>
# /mcp routes through a zag.detach worker; the toast appears once the worker
# notifies. Anchor on the toast header and the merge-only server name.
wait_text /MCP: / 8s
wait_text /jsonsrv/ 8s
snapshot after_mcp
send "/quit" <Enter>
wait_exit
